\fs24
\b CVScan SRS — Job Ingestion and Australian Job Search Layer\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Purpose\b0\par
This document defines the software requirements for the next CVScan scope: six high-impact user wins plus a three-stage Australian job search layer.\par
\par
\b 2. Scope\b0\par
In scope:\par
- Resume-to-job-match instant suggestions\par
- Paste job URL import\par
- Screenshot-to-job parser\par
- Apply / Stretch / Skip verdict\par
- Multi-source save into one tracker\par
- Duplicate job merging\par
- Step 1: Universal Job Inbox\par
- Step 2: Light Aggregation Layer\par
- Step 3: Unified CVScan Search Layer\par
\par
\b 3. Source of truth\b0\par
For implementation, docs/Build_Spec.md and any later docs/Build_Spec* files are the engineering source of truth. If this SRS conflicts with the Build Spec on sequencing or execution detail, the Build Spec governs.\par
\par
\b 4. Product objective\b0\par
CVScan should become the best candidate-side workflow for Australian job seekers by making it easy to capture jobs from anywhere, understand fit quickly, tailor application assets, and manage the full search in one place.\par
\par
\b 5. User segments\b0\par
- New graduates\par
- Career switchers\par
- International and visa candidates\par
- Active Australian job seekers using SEEK, Indeed, company sites, email alerts, and screenshots\par
\par
\b 6. Functional requirements\b0\par
\par
\b 6.1 Resume-to-job-match instant suggestions\b0\par
The system shall extract likely role targets, search terms, industries, and seniority from an uploaded or photographed resume.\par
The system shall present editable suggested searches immediately after resume parsing.\par
The system shall allow one-click saving of suggested searches.\par
\par
\b 6.2 Paste job URL import\b0\par
The system shall accept a job URL and create a structured job record.\par
The system shall extract title, company, location, description, requirements, source, salary if available, and application link if available.\par
The system shall let the user review and edit extracted fields before saving.\par
\par
\b 6.3 Screenshot-to-job parser\b0\par
The system shall accept image uploads from desktop and mobile.\par
The system shall perform OCR and extract a structured draft job record.\par
The system shall flag low-confidence fields and allow manual edits before save.\par
\par
\b 6.4 Apply / Stretch / Skip verdict\b0\par
The system shall evaluate the user profile against a saved job.\par
The system shall assign one of three verdicts: Apply, Stretch, or Skip.\par
The system shall provide plain-English reasons including matched requirements, missing must-haves, seniority mismatch, location issues, and visa mismatch where known.\par
The verdict shall not be presented as a guarantee of outcome.\par
\par
\b 6.5 Multi-source save into one tracker\b0\par
The system shall allow jobs to be saved from manual entry, pasted URLs, screenshots, future browser extension capture, future email forwarding, and future aggregation sources.\par
The system shall store all saved jobs in a single tracker with source badges and consistent statuses.\par
\par
\b 6.6 Duplicate job merging\b0\par
The system shall detect likely duplicate jobs using title, company, location, description, URL, and recency signals.\par
The system shall merge high-confidence duplicates into one canonical job record while preserving alternate source links.\par
The user shall be able to manually unmerge.\par
\par
\b 7. Job Search Layer\b0\par
\par
\b 7.1 Step 1 — Universal Job Inbox\b0\par
Goal: make CVScan the place where jobs from anywhere are collected and acted on.\par
Inputs: paste URL, upload screenshot, manual add.\par
Outputs: normalized job record, fit analysis, verdict, save to tracker, tailor action.\par
\par
\b 7.2 Step 2 — Light Aggregation Layer\b0\par
Goal: expand discovery using safer and maintainable sources.\par
Sources may include employer career pages, public structured job pages, approved partner feeds, user-imported email alerts, and company watchlists.\par
Unauthorized scraping of restricted platforms is out of scope.\par
\par
\b 7.3 Step 3 — Unified CVScan Search Layer\b0\par
Goal: provide a unified search interface over approved and normalized job data.\par
The system shall support filtering by location, remote type, salary, seniority, industry, source, and sponsorship if known.\par
The system shall support saved searches and alerts.\par
\par
\b 8. Common job schema\b0\par
Minimum fields: job_id, canonical_job_id, title, company_name, location_text, remote_type, employment_type, salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, job_description_raw, requirements_summary, source_type, source_name, source_url, alternate_source_urls, posted_at, discovered_at, extraction_method, parse_confidence, duplicate_confidence, status, and user_notes.\par
\par
\b 9. UX requirements\b0\par
- A single prominent Add Job entry point\par
- Clear review screen after parsing\par
- Verdict badge and reasoning\par
- Tracker with source, status, notes, and quick actions\par
- Resume upload flow that immediately suggests role targets and searches\par
\par
\b 10. Australian requirements\b0\par
The system should prioritize Australian location normalization, AUD salary formatting where possible, remote-in-Australia clarity, graduate and early-career relevance, and strong support for common Australian job seeking patterns.\par
\par
\b 11. Non-functional requirements\b0\par
- Secure storage for resumes, screenshots, and tracker data\par
- Access control on user records\par
- Auditability of source and extraction method\par
- Explainable verdicts and visible low-confidence extraction warnings\par
- Resilient ingestion where partial failures do not block manual correction and save\par
\par
\b 12. Success metrics\b0\par
- Time to first saved job\par
- Resume upload completion rate\par
- Jobs saved per active user\par
- Verdict view rate\par
- Tracker revisit rate\par
- Saved search usage\par
- Extraction success rate\par
- Duplicate merge precision\par
\par
\b 13. Recommended sequence\b0\par
Phase 1: resume suggestions, URL import, verdict.\par
Phase 2: screenshot parser, tracker source model, duplicate merging.\par
Phase 3: Universal Job Inbox polish, light aggregation, company watchlists.\par
Phase 4: unified search, ranking, saved searches, AU-first filters.\par
\par
\b 14. Acceptance summary\b0\par
This scope is complete when users can upload a resume, receive useful search suggestions, import jobs by URL and screenshot, save all jobs into one tracker, see Apply / Stretch / Skip verdicts, benefit from duplicate merging, and use a staged Australian job search layer.\par
}
